# External documents are identified by their working-tree bytes: the board hashes
# the file on disk, so a clone must check out exactly the bytes that were committed.
# Pin the checkout to LF everywhere instead of relying on the local core.autocrlf
# setting (global "true" would otherwise turn committed LF into CRLF on Windows).
# text=auto still lets Git detect binary content; the explicit binary rules below
# keep assets free of any text conversion.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
